[Music]  surfing for me is kind of a therapy it  brings a lot of joy and happiness  when creating one of our surfboards we  are making our own filament made from  locally collected plastic trash  this is how we can make the industry  sustainable and long-lasting  [Music]  my name is roman paul and i am the owner  of yuyu  i've been making surfboards for many  years now  the traditional way and we started this  business because  we experienced what we call the surface  paradox which is a major contradiction  between the eco-friendly mindset of most  surfers and the toxicity of the  equipment we use  regular surfboards the materials that  they're made of the polystyrene the  polyurethane the resins it's highly  pollutive they're not recyclable and all  of these materials are highly toxic and  we said this is not possible there must  be other ways to do this  we set up a new process which is based  on large format 3d printing and  bio-composite materials  when creating one of our surfboards it  all starts with the chat with the client  because each of our boards is made on  demand and based on on the surface needs  first we gather plastic trash from local  associations we work with  then we shrink it to make filament  and then we print the inner structure of  the board with a large format 3d printer  and then we laminate it with  bio-composite materials natural basil  fiber  combined with a plant-based bioresin  when the lamination is done we do the  paintings and the glassing and sanding  our surfboards do surf as well as a  regular surfboard it's even a little  better because you have this air inside  that acts like a floating carpet and it  enhances the experience  so we decided to adopt the 3d printing  technology because it enabled us  to use the materials we wanted in our  case recycled materials also to have a  local manufacturing process because it's  quite small so we can have everything  done at our workshop here in montpellier  in the south of france  and also we do not generate any other  waste we use only the strict amount of  materials that is necessary to make the  ball we don't cut anything and then we  realized that it also had tremendous  potentials in terms of ultra  personalization and also the search for  performance  being a small business owner is  difficult uh a challenge especially in  innovation because you have to be  convinced full convinced 200  in what you're doing and at the same  time be open to advice and new  technology and materials so we keep on  trying to improve what we do  i try to be an example for the industry  because small business is a choice for  us we think that uh we are heading  towards a new paradigm in industry with  micro production sites in different  parts of europe of uh in the world where  there is need for  recycling plastic and for  surfing  [Music]  for us it's our role as users of this  natural environment  to show that we can do things  differently and we can have more  sustainable and more responsible  behaviors  [Music]  you

